  "body": "## Problem and resulting behavior\n\nPrograms recomputed `IMUL_RCP` constants on every retirement. This adds a fully loaded immutable program image and optional once-per-admission preparation before the existing unsigned low64 multiply. Every reload is charged, including identical bytes and same-address replacement. Epoch/PC/error checks protect prepared packets; lexical no-ops, rounding, branches, memory and default runtime execution are preserved. Reset/whole cancel invalidate the image, execution cancellation retains it, and the legacy prepared-netlist ABI is rejected.\n\n## Evidence and experiment links\n\n[Design and complete evidence](https://github.com/jliu67/OpenRX/blob/35c2cae61092107acb2c684bbca308aca8fb280b/docs/validation/prepared-reciprocals/README.md) / [EXP-013](https://github.com/jliu67/OpenRX/blob/35c2cae61092107acb2c684bbca308aca8fb280b/experiments/EXP-013-prepared-program-reciprocals.md) / [server summary](https://github.com/jliu67/OpenRX/blob/35c2cae61092107acb2c684bbca308aca8fb280b/docs/validation/prepared-reciprocals/server/summary.json).\n\nRefs #69. The unchanged RandomX pin is `aaafe71322df6602c21a5c72937ac284724ae561`. Main 8f, draft65 exact4f and draft68 exacta4 plus all original sources/builds/data/receipts remain preserved. Complete outputs, commands, versions, native goldens, per-admission clocks, actual mapped netlists and effective kernel receipts are retained. Source work uses temporary snapshots and Git data API publication.\n\n## Validation\n\nAuthorized server command, inside fresh serialized resource admission:\n\n```sh\npython3 -B scripts/test_prepared_reciprocals.py --output /tmp/openrx-prepared-reciprocal-validation-UNIQUE --synthesize\n```\n\nEight Python accounting guards, 48 native iterations/12 admissions, 11 RTL checks, four mapped checks and three intentional invalid elaborations pass. Each integration profile checks 15,424 native retirements, 1,744 bytecode events, 384 tail stores and 12 complete final 2 MiB memories, including all no-op divisors/encodings, unsigned bit31 cases, register aliases, branch replay, replacement and cancellation. Final unexpected failures: 0. Four failed harness/synthesis attempts are retained. Four mapped PASS records exactly match RTL.\n\nMeasured preparation+execution clocks on the **directed native corpus**: ideal 370444\u2192159376; stalled 398580\u2192187512. Actual reciprocal occupancy is 66 clocks; preparation adds 70356, execution saves 281424, net 211068. Common phases/native work match; wait observers are nested costs. These are correctness-tested iteration-stage candidate measurements. Full-hash performance acceptance is skipped: initial hash/fill, program generation, actual dataset/calibrated memory, connected 8\u00d72048 prepared execution/interprogram/final hash and intended-core/physical PPA are missing. Separate draft65/68 stage costs remain contextual; complete-pipeline costs are null.\n\nActual Yosys 0.9 generic default mappings: baseline cache 75979 cells/24877 flops; prepared 152277/49640; guard 390/0, without unmapped cells. These cover new store/control and guard; complete prepared-backend mapping and physical SRAM/timing/power remain unexecuted. One serial worker uses the verified global lock, six affinity CPUs, CPU 600%, RAM 4 GiB/swap 512 MiB/Tasks128 and fresh reserve; observed peaks/counters are in the receipts.\n\n## Restored native and mapped regression gate\n\nThe previous head `1345db6d6abaf9d6a372b37325ec946eb870f56a` routed candidate CI to source/evidence checks and skipped inherited native/mapped integration. This successor removes the selector and its conditions. The existing `integer-differential` job now unconditionally executes `scripts/test_program_sequence.py --synthesize`; strict binding and rejection tests remain additional checks. Companion-job wording is scoped to that check. The declaration changes reason prose only; original accepted manifest and old/new digests retain their bytes, as do all 219 original scientific inputs. No RTL, oracle, workload or driver logic changes.\n\nFresh admitted server regression: **9 RTL / 9 mapped modes, 4 invalid parameter rejections and 3 actual generic synthesis targets pass; all mapped records equal RTL and all9RTL records equal preserved accepted component results. Forty-five positive commands complete rc0 with zero unexpected failures. Default whole-top mapping293370cells/13055flops; control-default19435/2551, control-short19443/2551 (Yosys0.9). Effective kernel peak7GiB RAM /1,597,886,464bytes swap; memory.max pressure2117, OOM/kill/throttling0; wall52min41.878s. The entire119,156,140-byte output archive is verified and retained on the authorized server with published inventory/checksum because it exceeds GitHub100MiB; no Git LFS/settings/install or release changes**. Exact default profile is eight programs \u00d7 four native iterations in v1/v2, ideal/stalled transport plus reset/cancel cases. Default 8\u00d72,048 control contract and bounded actual whole-top native gate validation are separately reported. `--full-v2` was not rerun. Every mapped PASS must exactly equal RTL; all three actual synthesis targets require generic-only cells and closing stat/JSON counts. Complete command/source/tool/input/output/resource records and archives are retained. [Regression evidence](https://github.com/jliu67/OpenRX/blob/35c2cae61092107acb2c684bbca308aca8fb280b/docs/validation/prepared-reciprocals/README.md#restored-integration-gate--2026-10-14).\n\nAll original, failed, skipped and successful source/output archives remain preserved, including the two earlier source-only hosted ZIPs, original skipped workflow/declaration and check records. This corrects the regression gate; it does not establish full-pipeline performance. Independent review must use this final exact head.\n\n## Persistent handoff\n\n- [x] STATE.md and HANDOFF.md current\n- [x] Consequential decisions and open questions recorded\n- [x] SESSION_LOG.md appended\n- [x] Vendor source and licenses preserved\n\nDraft for independent exact-head implementation and evidence review. No merge or full-hash performance acceptance is requested. Next prerequisite is a complete comparable pipeline baseline before multicontext, overlap, dual or wider issue work.\n",
